{"file":"Mathbox-3.1.0-v2.zip","bytes":224135,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"mathbox","description":"Sustained mathematical research with auditable claims, dependencies and reproducible experiments","version":"3.1.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/nidrissi/mathbox","homepage":"https://github.com/nidrissi/mathbox","keywords":["mathematics","research","proof-audit","literature","latex"]},{"path":".codex-plugin/plugin.json","name":"mathbox","description":"Sustained mathematical research with auditable claims, dependencies and reproducible experiments","version":"3.1.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/nidrissi/mathbox","homepage":"https://github.com/nidrissi/mathbox","keywords":["mathematics","research","proof-audit","literature","latex"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/computation-audit/SKILL.md","name":"computation-audit","description":"Design, run, or audit a mathematical computation that supports a research claim, including symbolic, exact, finite-field, representation-theoretic, homological, or numerical experiments. Use when correctness, provenance, tested range, reproducibility, or interpretation matters. Do not present bounded output as a universal proof.","headings":["Mathematical computation audit","Specify the contract","Audit the implementation","Run proportionately","Interpret conservatively","Persist and report"],"name_hint":"computation · 审查","description_zh":"设计、运行或审查支持数学研究主张的符号、精确、有限域、表示论、同调或数值计算，检查正确性、来源、范围、复现及解释，保留有界实验不能证明普遍结论的限制。"},{"path":"skills/literature-check/SKILL.md","name":"literature-check","description":"Verify an external mathematical theorem, citation, notation translation, source-dependent implication, or bounded novelty claim, reusing authorized project-local source copies when available. Use when a proof relies on a named paper/result, when exact hypotheses or versions matter, when the user asks whether a claim is known, or when an authenticated mathematical source should be cached for later checks. Prefer primary sources and record the search scope. Do not treat snippets or failed searches as proof or global novelty.","headings":["Mathematical literature check","Define the source question","Acquire and authenticate","Extract and translate","Novelty and overlap","Record and report"],"name_hint":"literature · 检查","description_zh":"核验外部数学定理、引文、符号转换、来源依赖推论及限定范围的新颖性，优先原始来源并记录检索范围，复用获授权本地资料；不把片段或检索失败当证明。"},{"path":"skills/manuscript-integrate/SKILL.md","name":"manuscript-integrate","description":"Integrate an already validated mathematical result, correction, citation, or referee response into an authoritative LaTeX manuscript while preserving hypotheses, evidence status, notation, and dependencies. Use only when the user explicitly requests manuscript integration. Do not use to invent a proof or to perform routine copyediting.","headings":["Manuscript integration","Preconditions","Build the integration map","Edit","Synchronize durable state","Verify","Report"],"name_hint":"manuscript · integrate","description_zh":"仅在明确要求时，将已验证数学结果、修正、引文或审稿回复整合至权威LaTeX手稿，保留假设、证据状态、符号与依赖；不用于发明证明或常规文字校对。"},{"path":"skills/proof-audit/SKILL.md","name":"proof-audit","description":"Adversarially audit an existing mathematical claim, proof, derivation, diagram, or theorem dependency for correctness. Use for requests to verify, referee, stress-test, type-check, find gaps, or isolate the exact remaining implication. Default to read-only. Do not use to invent a substantially new proof route or merely copyedit prose.","headings":["Mathematical proof audit","Establish the target","Build the dependency graph","Audit adversarially","Verdict","Output"],"name_hint":"proof · 审查","description_zh":"以默认只读方式对抗审查既有数学主张、证明、推导、图表或定理依赖，核验正确性并定位缺口及剩余推论；不用于创造新证明路线。"},{"path":"skills/proofread-math/SKILL.md","name":"proofread-math","description":"Conservatively proofread mathematical prose and LaTeX for grammar, typography, syntax, notation consistency, cross-references, and uniquely forced local mathematical typos. Use for explicit math-proofreading requests and final self-review of theorem-, proof-, or equation-heavy edits. Do not invent, replace, shorten, or substantively repair proofs.","headings":["Conservative mathematical proofreading","Select the mode","Workflow","Mathematical-token policy","Reviewer notes","Output"],"name_hint":"proofread · math","description_zh":"保守校对数学文字与LaTeX语法、排版、符号一致性、交叉引用及明确局部笔误，适用于显式校对和最终自查，不实质替换或修复证明。"},{"path":"skills/research-attempt/SKILL.md","name":"research-attempt","description":"Run one bounded, auditable mathematical research route: a proof attempt, reduction, counterexample search, source-dependent implication, or claim-supporting computation. Use when the user explicitly asks to attack a research question or invokes this skill. Do not use for a sustained multi-route investigation that continues after failed approaches, routine editing, explanation, or an unchanged verification rerun.","headings":["Bounded mathematical research attempt","Resolve project context","Open the route","Execute","Classify the outcome","Persist at a natural checkpoint","Verify and report"],"name_hint":"研究 · attempt","description_zh":"在明确研究请求下运行一次有边界、可审计的数学证明尝试、化简、反例搜索、来源推论或计算；不用于失败后持续多路线调查或常规解释。"},{"path":"skills/research-init/SKILL.md","name":"research-init","description":"Initialize or migrate an AI-assisted mathematical research repository's agent architecture. Use only when the user explicitly asks to set up, plan a retrofit, or substantially revise AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, live research status/history, workflow files, or their authority structure, including migrating a flat research log across programs into program indexes. Inspect first, propose a reviewable file plan, and default to no repository-local skills. Do not use for an ordinary research attempt, a closeout of one named program or phase, or a read-only project retrospective.","headings":["Mathematical research repository initializer","Non-negotiable behavior","Phase 1 — inspect read-only","Phase 2 — interview adaptively","Phase 3 — propose before writing","Existing instruction and live-state migration","Legacy research-log migration","Phase 4 — write the approved project layer","Skill-layer rule","Phase 5 — validate","Final report"],"name_hint":"研究 · init","description_zh":"在明确要求时初始化或迁移AI数学研究仓库的智能体架构、指令、状态历史和工作流，先检查并提出可评审文件计划，默认不建仓库本地技能。"},{"path":"skills/research-program/SKILL.md","name":"research-program","description":"Pursue or close out a substantial mathematical research program across multiple proof, counterexample, literature, and computational routes. Use when the user asks for sustained investigation, several approaches, continuation until a goal is reached, or an authorized closeout of one named program or phase that compacts its live status and history. Coordinate successive attempts and preserve their evidence. Do not use for a single bounded lemma attempt, ordinary explanation, proofreading, a read-only project retrospective, or a repository-wide migration of instructions or a flat research log into program indexes.","headings":["Sustained mathematical research","Establish the target once","Build and execute a diverse portfolio","Change direction on evidence","Audit candidate breakthroughs","Persist and report"],"name_hint":"研究 · program","description_zh":"跨证明、反例、文献和计算路线持续推进大型数学研究或获授权的指定阶段收尾，协调连续尝试并保留证据；单次引理、普通解释和仓库指令迁移使用其他流程。"},{"path":"skills/research-retrospective/SKILL.md","name":"research-retrospective","description":"Reconcile a mathematical research repository's current claims, proofs, computations, status, literature dependencies, and failed routes, then recommend the next bounded research moves. Use only when the user asks for a project review, weekly/monthly retrospective, prioritization, a prose project handoff, or “what should I do next?”. Do not use to write a program closeout, migrate research history, operate a .mathbox ledger, or generate its dependency-aware handoff. Default to read-only.","headings":["Research retrospective","Establish authority","Build the portfolio","Select next routes","Review the AI workflow","Output"],"name_hint":"研究 · 复盘","description_zh":"默认只读复盘数学研究仓库的当前主张、证明、计算、状态、文献依赖与失败路线，推荐下一项有界研究行动，支持周月复盘、优先级及文字交接。"},{"path":"skills/research-state/SKILL.md","name":"research-state","description":"Track exact mathematical claims, evidence revisions, dependency impact, audit provenance, research routes, and parallel or delayed executions in a local append-only ledger. Use when a project has a .mathbox ledger or the user asks for executable research-state tracking, stale-evidence detection, run reconciliation, or a dependency-aware handoff generated from recorded events. Do not initialize state for a casual math question, replace proof auditing with metadata validation, or write a prose project retrospective from status files.","headings":["Executable research state","Read before changing state","Record only material changes","Use routes to support decisions","Report and persist"],"name_hint":"研究 · state","description_zh":"在本地追加式.mathbox账本记录精确数学主张、证据版本、依赖影响、审查来源、研究路线及并行延迟执行，支持陈旧证据检查、运行核对和依赖交接，不以元数据替代证明审查。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Mathbox","What changes in v3","Quick start","Claude Code: install the plugin","Codex: install the plugin","Standalone or single-skill installation","Codex","Claude Code","Included plugin skills","Choosing a skill","Local literature cache","Updating and pinning","Repository structure","Verification","Contributing","License"]},{"path":"evals/README.md","headings":["Evaluating Mathbox","Independent task protocol","Raw fixtures"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".codex-plugin/plugin.json",".github/workflows/check.yml",".gitignore","AGENTS.md","LICENSE","README.md","assets/mathbox.svg","docs/design-v3.md","docs/validation-v3.md","evals/README.md","evals/cases.json","evals/fixtures/absolute-grading.md","eval